Client.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting longer before each retry.\n\n**What changed:**\n- `urlopen` raises an `HTTPError` for a 503. When that happens, the client waits `backoff * 2**attempt` seconds and tries again. With the default 0.5s, that's 0.5s, then 1s.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, the original `HTTPError` is raised so callers see the error the same way as before.\n- Any other HTTP error (404, 500, \u2026) is raised right away with no retry.\n- Network errors and timeouts (`URLError`) are not retried, because you only asked for 503.\n- The constructor takes a new optional argument, `backoff=0.5`, so tests can use a short wait. Existing callers don't need to change.\n\n**Checked against a real local HTTP server** (backoff set to 0.01s):\n- 503, 503, 200 \u2192 returned the JSON after 3 requests\n- 503, 503, 503 \u2192 raised `HTTPError 503` after 3 requests\n- 500 and 404 \u2192 raised after 1 request each\n\nThere's no test suite or git repo in this directory, so no test file was added. The check above was a one-off script.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34795, "requests_cache_write": 144159, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7623620000000001, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1728, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial16", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 90, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:49:41.902152+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.507, "t_checker_s": 2.379, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], 